{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>{{ site_name }} support &amp; FAQ</h1>
{% if support_email %}
<p class="lede">
  Questions, a wrong water name, or an alert that did not arrive: email
  <a href="mailto:{{ support_email }}">{{ support_email }}</a>.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="schedule">Where does the schedule come from?</h2>
<p>
  From the California Department of Fish and Wildlife's
  <a href="https://nrm.dfg.ca.gov/FishPlants/PublicPlantSearch">Fish Planting
  Schedule</a>, checked once a day. The schedule was last checked
  {{ source_fetched_label }}. CDFW updates it weekly and lists plants by
  <strong>week</strong>, never by day, on purpose. Plants are subject to
  change, so everything here is scheduled, not confirmed.
</p>

<h2 id="history">Why does this site show more weeks than CDFW's page?</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's page only shows about a year. This site keeps every week it has
  recorded, so a water's history keeps growing after CDFW's page has moved on.
</p>

<h2 id="calendar">How do I subscribe to a water's calendar?</h2>
<p>
  Every water page links to a calendar feed (.ics). Copy that link and add it
  as a subscribed calendar: on iPhone, in the Calendar app's settings under
  Add Account &rarr; Other &rarr; Add Subscribed Calendar; in Google
  Calendar, under Other calendars &rarr; From URL. Each event spans the whole
  week CDFW scheduled.
</p>

<h2 id="alerts">Why didn't the app alert me?</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Alerts are part of the one-time in-app purchase; favoriting and
      browsing are free.</li>
  <li>Notifications must be allowed for the app (Settings &rarr;
      Notifications).</li>
  <li>The app checks for a new schedule in the background, and iOS decides
      when that happens. Background App Refresh must be on for the app, Low
      Power Mode pauses it, and swiping the app away can stop it until you
      open it again.</li>
  <li>CDFW updates weekly, so an alert arrives within the week a water is
      added, not the minute it is.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="restore">How do I restore my purchase on a new phone?</h2>
<p>
  In the app, open About &rarr; Unlock full access &rarr; Restore purchases.
  Use the same Apple Account you bought it with. There is no account with
  this app to sign in to.
</p>

<h2 id="privacy">What does the app know about me?</h2>
<p>Nothing leaves your phone. See the <a href="{{ root }}privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
{% if ga4_measurement_id %}
<p>
  The website is different: it uses Google Analytics to count visits, unless
  your browser sends Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track, or you press
  &ldquo;Opt out of analytics&rdquo; at the bottom of any page. The app has
  no analytics.
</p>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
